<title>SPAIN: Hamburgische LB expands its 4-yr matador.</title>
<headline>Hamburgische LB expands its 4-yr matador.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hamburgische Landesbank has increased its four-year matador issue by 5.0 billion pesetas ($32.2 million) to 15 billion pesetas, joint lead manager Argentaria Banco de Negocios said on Monday.</p>
<p>The issue price for the five billion will be 100.90.</p>
<p>The other joint-lead managers are Banco Urquijo, BBV and BNP.  </p>
<p>The following give details of the matador:</p>
<p>Issuer: Hamburgische Landesbank Girozentrale.</p>
<p>Total Volume:  15.0 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>Coupon: 5.44 percent.</p>
<p>Expiry: 10/9/01.</p>
<p>Issue price: 100.90.</p>
<p>Repayment price: par.</p>
<p>Payment date: 10/9/97.</p>
<p>Nominal: 100.00 pesetas.</p>
<p>Coupon payment:Annual.</p>
<p>IBCA rating: AAA.</p>
<p>Total commission: 1 percent.</p>
<p>NOTE: Argentaria said commissions for the 5.0 billion peseta increase would rise to 1.10 percent. The issue is callable on September 10, 1998 at par.</p>
</text>
